PORT=3001

# ─── Database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Must point at the NON-OWNER runtime role. Owners bypass their own row level
# security policies unless the table is FORCEd, and every tenancy guarantee in
# this system assumes a non-owner connection — `auth/db.ts` says so and
# `db/__tests__/tenant-isolation.test.ts` measures the difference.
#
# On a cluster where `tmm_app` has no LOGIN (the usual local shape, since
# `0000_baseline.sql` creates it NOLOGIN and the api test suite's global
# teardown drops it), connect as the owner and set the role at connection
# start — the same `options=-c role=tmm_app` trick `src/test/db-harness.ts`
# uses, which makes `current_user` `tmm_app` from the first statement:
#
#   DATABASE_URL=postgres://you@localhost:5432/postgres?options=-c%20role%3Dtmm_app
DATABASE_URL=postgres://tmm_app@localhost:5432/postgres

# ─── Better Auth ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# At least 32 bytes: `openssl rand -base64 32`. Signs session cookies and
# verification tokens — the server refuses to boot without it.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=generate-me-openssl-rand-base64-32
# The origin the BROWSER loads the app from, NOT this process's listen address.
# Better Auth derives `trustedOrigins` from it; pointing it at the API's own
# port makes every sign-in a 403 INVALID_ORIGIN. Defaults to the Vite dev
# server when unset.
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:5173

# ─── Postmark (email delivery) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Create a server at https://account.postmarkapp.com — copy the Server API Token here.
# Each town can override this with a per-town token in town_notification_config.
POSTMARK_SERVER_TOKEN=your-postmark-server-api-token

# ─── App URL (used in email links) ─────────────────────────────────────────
APP_URL=http://localhost:5173

# ─── Postmark Setup Notes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Message streams required on your Postmark server:
#   1. "outbound"  (transactional) — invites, password resets, minutes review, admin alerts
#   2. "broadcast" (broadcast)     — meeting notices, agenda/minutes published
#
# Sender domain:
#   - Verify *.townmeetingmanager.com in Postmark (Sender Signatures → Domain)
#   - Add the SPF, DKIM, and DMARC DNS records Postmark provides
#   - Each town sender (notifications@townname.townmeetingmanager.com) is then valid
